id: insurance
name: Insurance - policies and claims
industry: Insurance
domain: General and life insurance: products, policies, premiums and claims
scope: Parties and intermediaries, insurance products and coverages, quotes and policies, insured objects, premiums, endorsements and renewals, claims, assessment, reserves and settlements, reinsurance cessions.
summary: Describes what an insurer sells, who and what is insured under a policy, what premium is charged, and how a claim is notified, assessed and settled. A starter model for policy administration, claims analytics and regulatory reporting.
purpose: Shared vocabulary across policy administration, claims and distribution systems.
read: An Insurance product offers Coverages. A Quote may become a Policy issued to a Policyholder, sold by an Intermediary, covering Insured objects with Policy coverages at a sum insured, for a Premium. Endorsements change a policy. A Claim is made on a policy for a Loss event, assessed by an Adjuster, reserved and settled through Claim payments.
in: Parties and intermediaries; Products and coverages; Policies, premiums, endorsements; Claims and settlement; Reinsurance
out: Investment management; Actuarial model internals; HR and commissions accounting detail
std: acord | high | Party, policy, coverage and claim concepts follow the ACORD Reference Architecture. | Policy, Coverage, Claim, Insured, Insurer, Premium, Endorsement
std: fibo | low | Legal entities and contracts follow FIBO foundations. | LegalEntity, Contract
std: schema | low | People and organisations are aligned to schema.org. | schema:Person, schema:Organization
== Party | Parties | Who is involved.
Party | A person or organisation involved in an insurance contract or claim.
  - name : string !
  - contact number : string
  - email : string
Policyholder : Party | The party that buys the policy and owes the premium.
  - customer number : string !
InsuredPerson : Party | A person whose life or health is covered.
  - date of birth : date
  - gender : string
Beneficiary : Party | The party entitled to receive the benefit.
  - share percent : decimal
Intermediary : Party | An agent, broker or bank that sells policies for the insurer.
  - licence number : string !
  > of type > IntermediaryType 1
IntermediaryType | The kind of distribution partner.
  * Agent, Broker, Bancassurance, Direct, Web aggregator
Adjuster : Party | A person who investigates and values a claim.
== Product | Products | What is sold.
InsuranceProduct | An insurance offering with defined coverages and rating rules.
  - product code : string !
  - product name : string !
  > in line of business > LineOfBusiness 1
  > offers > Coverage +
LineOfBusiness | The class of insurance.
  * Motor, Health, Property, Life, Crop, Travel, Liability, Marine
Coverage | A type of protection against a defined peril or loss.
  - coverage code : string !
  - coverage name : string !
  - description : string
== Policy | Policies | The contract.
Quote | A priced offer of insurance that has not yet been accepted.
  - quote number : string !
  - quoted on : date !
  - quoted premium : decimal
  - valid until : date
  > for product > InsuranceProduct 1
  > requested by > Party 1
Policy | The insurance contract in force between the insurer and the policyholder.
  - policy number : string !
  - issued on : date !
  - effective from : date !
  - effective to : date !
  - total sum insured : decimal
  > issued to > Policyholder 1 | | holds policy
  > of product > InsuranceProduct 1
  > sold by > Intermediary ?
  > converted from > Quote ?
  > renews > Policy ? | The previous term this policy continues.
  > has status > PolicyStatus 1
  > covers object > InsuredObject *
  > covers person > InsuredPerson *
  > names beneficiary > Beneficiary *
PolicyStatus | The state of a policy.
  * In force, Lapsed, Cancelled, Expired, Renewed
PolicyCoverage | One coverage as bought on a policy, with its limit and deductible.
  - sum insured : decimal !
  - deductible : decimal
  - coverage premium : decimal
  > on policy > Policy 1 | | has coverage
  > of coverage > Coverage 1
InsuredObject | A thing that is insured, such as a vehicle, building or crop.
  - description : string !
  - declared value : decimal
  - identifier : string | Registration number, address or survey number.
  > of type > InsuredObjectType 1
InsuredObjectType | The kind of thing insured.
  * Vehicle, Building, Contents, Crop, Livestock, Cargo, Equipment
Premium | An amount charged for a policy for a period.
  - due on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  - tax amount : decimal
  - paid on : date
  > for policy > Policy 1
Endorsement | An agreed change to a policy during its term.
  - endorsement number : string !
  - effective on : date !
  - description : string
  - premium change : decimal
  > changes > Policy 1
== Claim | Claims | When a loss happens.
LossEvent | An occurrence that causes loss, such as an accident, illness or storm.
  - occurred on : dateTime !
  - location : string
  - description : string
  > of cause > CauseOfLoss 1
CauseOfLoss | The peril that caused the loss.
  * Accident, Theft, Fire, Flood, Illness, Death, Drought, Third-party liability
Claim | A request for payment under a policy for a loss.
  - claim number : string !
  - notified on : date !
  - claimed amount : decimal
  - closed on : date
  > made on > Policy 1 | | has claim
  > under coverage > PolicyCoverage *
  > arising from > LossEvent 1
  > made by > Party 1
  > has status > ClaimStatus 1
  > assessed by > Adjuster ?
ClaimStatus | The stage of a claim.
  * Notified, Under assessment, Approved, Rejected, Settled, Reopened
ClaimAssessment | The adjuster's finding on liability and amount.
  - assessed on : date !
  - assessed amount : decimal
  - liability admitted : boolean
  - remarks : string
  > of claim > Claim 1
ClaimReserve | Money set aside for the expected cost of an open claim.
  - reserved on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > for claim > Claim 1
ClaimPayment | A payment made to settle a claim in full or in part.
  - paid on : date !
  - amount : decimal !
  > settles > Claim 1
  > paid to > Party 1
ReinsuranceCession | The share of a policy's risk passed to a reinsurer.
  - ceded percent : decimal !
  - reinsurer : string !
  - treaty reference : string
  > cedes > Policy 1
rule: constraint | Loss within cover | A claim is payable only if the loss event occurred between the policy's effective dates. | Claim, Policy, LossEvent
rule: constraint | Limit | Total claim payments under a policy coverage cannot exceed its sum insured less deductible. | ClaimPayment, PolicyCoverage
rule: derivation | Loss ratio | Loss ratio is claim payments plus reserves divided by earned premium. | Claim, Premium
rule: constraint | Premium before cover | A policy is in force only once its first premium is paid. | Policy, Premium
uc: Loss ratio by product and intermediary | Underwriting head | What is the loss ratio by line of business and by intermediary? | Policy, InsuranceProduct, LineOfBusiness, Intermediary, Claim, ClaimPayment, Premium | of product, in line of business, sold by, made on, settles, for policy, ClaimPayment.amount, Premium.amount
uc: Claims open too long | Claims manager | Which claims have been under assessment for more than 30 days? | Claim, ClaimStatus, Adjuster | Claim.notified on, Claim.has status, assessed by
uc: Policies due for renewal | Retention team | Which in-force policies expire next month and who sold them? | Policy, PolicyStatus, Policyholder, Intermediary | Policy.effective to, Policy.has status, issued to, sold by
